        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: взлетать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "взлетать (vzletát) — \"to take off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Самолёт медленно взлетает над морем. Samolyót médlenno vzletáyet nad mórem. The plane slowly takes off over the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective взлететь (взлечу, взлетишь). Вз- means up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "взлетать (vzletát) is built from вз- 'up' and летать 'to fly'. EtymDB lists the noun взлёт (vzlyot) from Proto-Slavic vŭzletŭ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
